 look for other supplicants. She hired a younger woman to help her dispense the many tantalizing goodies. The process of pleasing both Don Jose and his sexual proclivity had gone on for many years. Soon after, when Sor María became older and wearier of the demands of her husband, she made her closer to her as an assistant. She gave her a bracelet of very fine gemstones. One time she went out of the house when her husband was gone and said to the others;
„Well, ladies, our darling Don Jose is off with his mother-in-law, and a trip to the Isla de Maravillas‟. They all laughed.
„That‟s where he makes his rounds among the fairer sex. We must carry on like we usually do and we must remain alert. The other day one of my daughters came and so did her swaggerer. Those two got into a tussle in the foyer. They were swearing and making moans, and then her lover left so no fun for her. I hope there aren‟t too many troubles from some miscreants. I would rather not be upset.‟ Then she said,

 visit him. The moment she walked into his room he stood up abruptly leaving her in such confu- sion. As the confu-sion dawned into reality she rushed to him fearing he could be unwell. She held his clenched fists and whispered, “Why are you tensing up? What’s wrong? What’s happened?” She clung onto his arms as she yelled at him. No sooner had she quietened him down than he mumbled words that pierced her ears. “Tell mom I will be back tonight, not to worry.”  

These words didn’t make any sense to her, why, who was this person who was mumbling?  

“What do you mean, you will be back tonight?” “I just meant this bed is so uncomfortable, I want to go back to my own bed tonight.” “Go back to your own bed? What are you saying?” “You know, Chain Head Cubby’s bed, isn’t it?” “Oh, you mean Bobby.” “Yes, Bobby. I’ll be back tonight in Bobby’s bed.” “Are you sure you heard me, Bobby?” “Yeah, for sure.” “But this is inconceivable;

 tell him exactly how she felt, {“leave me alone.”} She had absolutely no desire to persist in the ridiculous conversation. But she could not help herself and she would say, {“So, you want to learn to avoid me… Well, I am going to teach you how.”}

Jane was so controlled by her desire to do something to bring him down, that she could not hear all that he had to say. She wanted to shove him down, put him in jail, turn him over to the nearest women's shelter. But she didn't let herself show those feelings. No, their conversation wasn't over yet.

Jane found herself saying, {“I don't know why I even bother listening to this whack job.”}

Dr. asked, {“I understand, and I want to assure you, I cannot help. It's one thing to listen, another to take action.”}

Jane raised her voice, {“Oh, please, Dad.”}

